# THE GAME's environment. Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your
# values - `dotenvy` resolves `.env` from the process WORKING DIRECTORY,
# which for the game is the deployment root (this directory).
#
# Split from the single combined `.env.example` on 2026-09-08, when the
# bot moved out of the workspace root into `bot/`. The bot's half is
# `bot/.env.example`; the two are disjoint, and no key appears in both.

# Which login holds the operator gates on the game's web dashboard:
# /admin/tunables, /admin/passives, the operator encounter trigger, the
# unfiltered /fights list, and the Operator tier on replay bundles. All
# five follow this one key, deliberately - a typo in one of several keys
# would leave the operator holding some surfaces and locked out of the
# rest. Compared case-insensitively; the value is lowercased on read.
#
# Leave unset for lokati_gaming, the value these gates were hardcoded to
# before this key existed. Changing it needs only a restart, not a
# rebuild. Point it at an account that EXISTS and has been logged into
# successfully before relying on it - loading /admin/tunables as that
# account is the check.
#
# Whatever this is set to is also refused at local registration, so a
# player can never claim the operator's name. `lokati_gaming` stays
# reserved regardless of this value.
OPERATOR_LOGIN=

# Local port for the game's own web dashboard (character management,
# crafting, the passive tree, /admin/*). Defaults to 4005 when unset -
# game/src/main.rs:106.
ADVENTURE_WEB_PORT=4005

# Local port for the game's OBS fight overlay. Defaults to 4004 when
# unset - game/src/main.rs:107. Point an OBS Browser Source at
# http://localhost:<this port>/.
ADVENTURE_OVERLAY_SERVER_PORT=4004

# Base directory every persisted game file resolves against - character
# saves, world state, live-tunables/item-balance TOML, migration markers,
# logs. Leave UNSET for production, which is what production runs today:
# unset falls back to an EMPTY base, so every path stays exactly
# CWD-relative and the deployment root IS the data directory. Set it only
# to point a second instance at its own data (see
# game/src/adventure/paths.rs). Changing it on a live deployment strands
# the existing data at the old location.
# GAME_DATA_DIR=

# One-time escape hatch for standing up a NEW deployment: carries the
# LOGIN to allow through registration, not a boolean. OPERATOR_LOGIN's
# gate refuses to register the operator's own name, which means a fresh
# instance cannot create the account its gates point at - Linux staging
# needed a source patch to get past that once. Set it to the operator
# login, register that account, then REMOVE it; it is read live, so
# removing it takes effect without a restart. It does not pierce the
# permanent reserved-name list (adventure_web/accounts.rs:391).
# OPERATOR_BOOTSTRAP=
